+# pull_request_target runs this file from the base branch, never the PR's copy.
+# A pull_request run executes the workflow file from the PR head, so a PR
+# author could edit the ownership check below and have the bot approve the PR.
+#
+# SAFETY: this job is API-only. NEVER add actions/checkout, and never run,
+# install, or build anything from the PR head in this workflow. Fork PRs are
+# skipped at the job level and are never auto-approved. Never put untrusted PR
+# data (titles, branch names, filenames, logins) in a ${{ }} expression in any
+# step input that runs as code: run:, and also the github-script script: below.
+# Read that data from context.payload or the API inside the script.
+#
+# Approval lifecycle: stale events exit without changing reviews. A current run
+# withdraws this workflow's earlier approvals, evaluates an immutable comparison,
+# then re-checks the head and base and approves only as its last step.
+# A run that fails or is cancelled during the withdrawal can leave an
+# older approval on the PR, and a cancelled run's approval can land late. The
+# approval is pinned to the head commit that was checked, and ag-ui's "dismiss
+# stale approvals" branch rule dismisses it on a new push. "edited" covers a
+# change of the PR's base branch.
